Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Docker Permission Denied
If you encounter permission issues with Docker:

# Add user to docker group and restart session
sudo usermod -aG docker $USER
newgrp docker

# Or use sudo for docker commands temporarily
sudo docker ps
Issue 2: Port Already in Use
If ports are already in use:

# Check what's using the port
sudo netstat -tulpn | grep :5000

# Kill processes using the port
sudo fuser -k 5000/tcp

# Or use different ports in the playbooks
Issue 3: Ansible Connection Issues
If Ansible cannot connect to localhost:

# Test Ansible connectivity
ansible -i inventory/hosts.yml all -m ping

# Check Python interpreter
ansible -i inventory/hosts.yml all -m setup | grep ansible_python
Issue 4: Container Startup Failures
If containers fail to start:

# Check container logs
docker logs <container_name>

# Check available resources
docker system df
docker system prune -f

# Restart Docker service
sudo systemctl restart docker
